    answer:
      'Yes, though the structure matters. One common approach is a life estate deed, where the parent retains a life estate (the right to live in the property until death) and the child receives the remainder interest. Life estate deeds have their own Medicaid implications and tax consequences — consult an elder law attorney before proceeding.',
  },
