      'Florida Medicaid may assess a penalty period for transfers for less than fair market value during the lookback period, unless an exemption or other rule applies. The penalty period is calculated using the applicable state divisor, which changes periodically. An elder law attorney can evaluate whether there are strategies to mitigate the lookback exposure before the transfer occurs.',
  },
