    />
    <ProcessStep
      number={2}
      title="Determine documentary stamp obligation"
      description="If the property is subject to an outstanding mortgage, lien, or other encumbrance, calculate stamps on the outstanding balance at $0.70 per $100. If it is a clean gift with genuinely no consideration and no encumbrance, documentary stamps are generally not owed — but confirm against Fla. Stat. § 201.02 and DOR Rule 12B-4.013 if there is any ambiguity."
    />
    <ProcessStep
      number={3}
      title="Sign with two witnesses and a notary"
      description="The grantor must sign in the presence of two witnesses and a notary. The grantee is not required to be present for execution of a Florida quitclaim deed."
    />
    <ProcessStep
      number={4}
      title="Record the deed with the county clerk"
      description="Bring the original executed deed and any applicable recording fees to the clerk of court in the county where the property is located."
    />
    <ProcessStep
      number={5}
      title="File for new homestead exemption"
      description="If the recipient plans to occupy the property as their primary residence, contact the county property appraiser's office to apply before March 1 of their first year of ownership."
    />
    <ProcessStep
      number={6}
      title="Report the gift if required"
      description="A transfer may require Form 709 when the taxable gift exceeds the available annual exclusion or another federal reporting rule applies. Review current IRS filing requirements for the specific transfer."
    />
    <ProcessStep
      number={7}
      title="Consult an elder law attorney if Medicaid is a concern"
      description="If the owner may seek Medicaid long-term-care benefits within the applicable lookback period, seek legal advice before the deed is signed — not after."
      isLast={true}
    />
  </div>

  <CitableAnswerBlock
    question="Does a Florida quitclaim deed between family members trigger taxes?"
    answer="Possibly two kinds. Federally, if the property's value exceeds the annual gift tax exclusion ($19,000 per donee for 2026 — verify at IRS.gov), the excess is reported on Form 709 and typically reduces the donor's remaining lifetime exclusion. In Florida, documentary stamp tax ($0.70 per $100) applies to any outstanding mortgage or encumbrance on the transferred property, whether assumed or not; a clean gift with genuinely no consideration and no encumbrance generally owes none."
    source="Fla. Stat. §201.02; IRS.gov — Estate and Gift Tax (Last Verified: August 2026)"
  />

